.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_ADD_CERT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_add_cert ,
.Nm X509_add_certs
.Nd X509 certificate list addition functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509.h
.Ft int
.Fo X509_add_cert
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509) *sk"
.Fa "X509 *cert"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_add_certs
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509) *sk"
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509) *certs"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_add_cert
adds a certificate
.Fa cert
to the given list
.Fa sk .
It is an error for the
.Fa cert
argument to be NULL.
.Pp
.Fn X509_add_certs
adds a list of certificate
.Fa certs
to the given list
.Fa sk .
The
.Fa certs
argument may be NULL, which implies no effect.
It does not modify the list
.Fa certs
but in case the
.Sy X509_ADD_FLAG_UP_REF
flag (described below) is set the reference counters of those of its
members added to
.Fa sk
are increased.
.Pp
Both these functions have a
.Fa flags
parameter, which is used to control details of the operation.
.Pp
The value
.Sy X509_ADD_FLAG_DEFAULT ,
which equals 0, means no special semantics.
.Pp
If
.Sy X509_ADD_FLAG_UP_REF
is set then the reference counts of those certificates added
successfully are increased.
.Pp
If
.Sy X509_ADD_FLAG_PREPEND
is set then the certificates are prepended to
.Fa sk .
By default they are appended to
.Fa sk .
In both cases the original order of the added certificates is preserved.
.Pp
If
.Sy X509_ADD_FLAG_NO_DUP
is set then certificates already contained in
.Fa sk ,
which is determined using
.Xr X509_cmp 3 ,
are ignored.
.Pp
If
.Sy X509_ADD_FLAG_NO_SS
is set then certificates that are marked self-signed, which is
determined using
.Xr X509_self_signed 3 ,
are ignored.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Both functions return 1 for success and 0 for failure.
.Sh NOTES
If
.Fn X509_add_certs
is used with the flags
.Sy X509_ADD_FLAG_NO_DUP
or
.Sy X509_ADD_FLAG_NO_SS
it is advisable to use also
.Sy X509_ADD_FLAG_UP_REF
because otherwise likely not for all members of the
.Fa certs
list the ownership is transferred to the list of certificates
.Fa sk .
.Pp
Care should also be taken in case the
.Fa certs
argument equals
.Fa sk .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr X509_cmp 3
.Xr X509_self_signed 3
.Sh HISTORY
The functions
.Fn X509_add_cert
and
.Fn X509_add_certs
were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
